spec:
Consider the following adder-subtractor with a zero flag:

  synthesis verilog_input_version verilog_2001
  module TopModule (
      input do_sub,
      input [7:0] a,
      input [7:0] b,
      output reg [7:0] out,
      output reg result_is_zero
  );

      always @(*) begin
          case (do_sub)
            0: out = a+b;
            1: out = a-b;
          endcase

          if (~out)
              result_is_zero = 1;
      end

  endmodule

Unfortunately, this module has a bug. Implement a new version of this
module that fixes the bug.

final_design:
module TopModule (
    input do_sub,
    input [7:0] a,
    input [7:0] b,
    output reg [7:0] out,
    output reg result_is_zero
);

    always @(*) begin
        case (do_sub)
            1'b0: out = a + b;
            1'b1: out = a - b;
            default: out = 8'b0;
        endcase

        if (out == 8'b0)
            result_is_zero = 1'b1;
        else
            result_is_zero = 1'b0;
    end

endmodule

